foundation.question_text:
The graph shows the depth of water at a boat ramp over $24$ hours, with the mean position drawn as a dashed line. Use the graph to state the maximum depth and the time of the first low tide after midnight.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=11cm,height=6.5cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-0.8,xmax=26,ymin=0,ymax=11.5,xtick={0,2,...,24},ytick={0,1,...,11},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$t$ (hours after midnight)},ylabel={Depth (m)},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:24,samples=200] {3*cos(30*x)+7};
\addplot[dashed,domain=0:24,samples=2] {7};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
The graph shows the air temperature in a valley over $24$ hours, with the mean position of $21^{\circ}$C drawn as a dashed line. Use the graph to find how many of the $24$ hours have a temperature above the mean position.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=11cm,height=6.5cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-0.8,xmax=26,ymin=0,ymax=30,xtick={0,2,...,24},ytick={0,3,...,27},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$t$ (hours after midnight)},ylabel={Temperature ($^{\circ}$C)},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:24,samples=200] {6*sin(15*x)+21};
\addplot[dashed,domain=0:24,samples=2] {21};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
